      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "Find the value of \\( x \\) at which \\( f \\) attains its absolute maximum on the closed interval \\( 0 \\le x \\le 4 \\). Justify your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "x = 3",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "The only critical point in the interval is x = 3, so the candidates are the endpoints and x = 3.",
               "latex": "f(0) = -3, \\; f(3) = 6e^{-3}, \\; f(4) = 13e^{-4}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Compare the two positive values, using e > 13/6.",
               "latex": "6e^{-3} - 13e^{-4} = e^{-4}(6e - 13) > 0"
